    {
      "id": "6656178",
      "title": "Using HostBinding to Bind to Host Properties",
      "lectureOrder": 421,
      "videoOrder": 387,
      "sourceHash": "7cd685d6ae16b9ebcddb72c8b23bd616cad91729b867c95898dd8230a3ffb981",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.64,
          "end": 4.74,
          "en": "-: So we learned about host listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.74,
          "end": 7.907,
          "en": "and this setup here is absolutely fine for what we're doing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.907,
          "end": 12.088,
          "en": "but we got another decorator we can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.088,
          "end": 15.63,
          "en": "which then allows us to not use the renderer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.63,
          "end": 18.019,
          "en": "There is nothing wrong with using the renderer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.019,
          "end": 20.52,
          "en": "but we got an even easier way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.52,
          "end": 22.38,
          "en": "of simply changing the background color",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.38,
          "end": 24.78,
          "en": "if that is all we want to do in the directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.78,
          "end": 28.05,
          "en": "Again, using the renderer is not wrong though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.05,
          "end": 33.05,
          "en": "The decorator I'm referring to is called at host binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.6,
          "end": 36.63,
          "en": "which also needs to be imported from at Angular core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.63,
          "end": 38.4,
          "en": "And since we get a lot of imports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.4,
          "end": 41.549,
          "en": "I'll quickly restructure this to cover multiple lines.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.549,
          "end": 44.895,
          "en": "So host binding, that's the new decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.895,
          "end": 48.547,
          "en": "and I will come back to what we pass here in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.547,
          "end": 52.92,
          "en": "First of all, we need to bind this to some property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.92,
          "end": 56.31,
          "en": "which value will become important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.31,
          "end": 59.91,
          "en": "So that could be a background color property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.91,
          "end": 63.16,
          "en": "a new property I create here, which is of type string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.16,
          "end": 67.145,
          "en": "Now in host binding, we can pass a string defining",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.145,
          "end": 72.145,
          "en": "to which property of the hosting element we want to bind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.973,
          "end": 76.62,
          "en": "Now, properties of the hosting element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.62,
          "end": 79.17,
          "en": "that is simply what we also access here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.17,
          "end": 81.144,
          "en": "in the basic highlight directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81.144,
          "end": 83.7,
          "en": "Style would be such a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.7,
          "end": 86.861,
          "en": "And there then the background color property to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.861,
          "end": 91,
          "en": "Therefore, we can simply say style dot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91,
          "end": 94.643,
          "en": "And now camel case background color and that's all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.643,
          "end": 97.2,
          "en": "Camel case is important here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 97.2,
          "end": 99.6,
          "en": "because we're accessing the Dom property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.6,
          "end": 102.36,
          "en": "which doesn't know dashes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.36,
          "end": 107.22,
          "en": "So with this, what we're telling Angular is on the element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 107.22,
          "end": 111.45,
          "en": "this directive sits, please access the style property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.45,
          "end": 115.28999999999999,
          "en": "which pretty much any input has on our directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.28999999999999,
          "end": 116.88,
          "en": "which access something like the value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.88,
          "end": 118.989,
          "en": "You of course have to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.989,
          "end": 121.165,
          "en": "that they are only added to inputs which have this property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.165,
          "end": 124.26,
          "en": "But here again the style property should be available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.26,
          "end": 125.7,
          "en": "on any element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.7,
          "end": 128.04,
          "en": "So here we access the style property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.04,
          "end": 131.31,
          "en": "and then there a sub property, the background color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.31,
          "end": 132.48,
          "en": "And we set this equal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.48,
          "end": 135.00900000000001,
          "en": "to whatever background color is set to here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.00900000000001,
          "end": 137.97,
          "en": "Well, and we can simply change background color here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.97,
          "end": 139.62,
          "en": "when we mouse over it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.62,
          "end": 144.62,
          "en": "We can set background color to blue in this case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.784,
          "end": 150.48,
          "en": "and set it transparent in this case here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 150.48,
          "end": 153.99,
          "en": "Transparent and I will comment out the render code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 153.99,
          "end": 155.73,
          "en": "Again, not wrong to use it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.73,
          "end": 157.603,
          "en": "but no longer need it in this example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.603,
          "end": 161.07,
          "en": "Of course, we also have to set some initial color",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 161.07,
          "end": 162.65699999999998,
          "en": "so that we don't get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.65699999999998,
          "end": 166.29,
          "en": "before we mouse over it the first time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.29,
          "end": 168.93,
          "en": "So here I will set this to transparent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 168.93,
          "end": 171.617,
          "en": "Initially, give this initial value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 171.617,
          "end": 176.483,
          "en": "With this it's transparent, no error looks good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 176.483,
          "end": 180.48,
          "en": "And if we hover over it, it works the same way as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 180.48,
          "end": 183.69,
          "en": "but now solely driven through host listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183.69,
          "end": 184.675,
          "en": "and host binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 184.675,
          "end": 186.9,
          "en": "A great way for working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 186.9,
          "end": 189.27,
          "en": "with the element inside of a directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 189.27,
          "end": 192.03,
          "en": "And of course, here on host binding, you can bind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 192.03,
          "end": 195.003,
          "en": "to any property of the element you're sitting on.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
